BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:States of Anxiety\, States of Hope | Works of Inez Storer
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260312T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260418T160000
UID:762728e0b5ceb0d9badc0a0a78d239d5@petalumaartscenter.org
DESCRIPTION:[ { "shape": "underline"\, "isFront": false\, "isAnimationEnab
 led": false\, "animation": "draw"\, "duration": 0.5\, "direction": "right"
 \, "color": { "type": "THEME_COLOR" }\, "thickness": { "unit": "em"\, "val
 ue": 0.1 }\, "linecap": "square"\, "type": "highlight"\, "id": "481f9063-c
 358-4f54-ba25-2bb0e1e78086" }\, { "shape": "underline"\, "isFront": false\
 , "isAnimationEnabled": false\, "animation": "draw"\, "duration": 0.5\, "d
 irection": "right"\, "color": { "type": "THEME_COLOR" }\, "thickness": { "
 unit": "em"\, "value": 0.1 }\, "linecap": "square"\, "type": "highlight"\,
  "id": "b6b0b557-4e51-4704-9d2c-6f9a8066a92b" } ] States of Anxiety\, Stat
 es of Hope Exhibition Dates: March 12 - April 18\, 2026 Opening Reception:
  Thursday\, March 12\, 5:30-7:30pm States of Anxiety\, States of Hope &nbs
 p\;presents a selection of works by artist Inez Storer that reflect on the
  emotional\, cultural\, and political complexities of contemporary life. B
 uilding on themes explored in &nbsp\; Americana Reimagined \, &nbsp\;Store
 r’s paintings offer a layered meditation on identity\, memory\, and coll
 ective experience in times of uncertainty and transformation. Through her 
 distinctive magical realist collage method\, Storer constructs richly text
 ured visual narratives that merge personal history with broader social rea
 lities. Her works are composed of fragments—symbols\, images\, and artif
 acts drawn from her life and interests. Storer's paintings guide the viewe
 r on a journey through both historical memory and internal landscapes. The
 y balance darkness and light\, anxiety and hope.&nbsp\; She asks us to ref
 lect on the conditions of our moment. States of Anxiety\, States of Hope a
 ffirms art’s capacity to illuminate struggle while nurturing resilience\
 , empathy\, and connection. Biography Storer lives in Inverness\, Californ
 ia\, and has a studio in Point Reyes Station. Born in Santa Monica in 1933
  to a Catholic father and Jewish mother\, she spent time on Hollywood movi
 e sets where her father worked as an art director. Influenced by stage des
 ign\, her work often creates a sense of “theatrical space” and reflect
 s her ancestry. Shortly before her death\, her mother revealed that she ha
 d fled Germany to escape Nazism. Storer later learned of cousins who escap
 ed on the Kindertransport. The frustration of being kept from the truth ha
 s infused her work with a distinct angst. Her work is held in many collect
 ions including the Jewish Museum in New York\, Manetti Shrem Museum of Art
  at UC Davis\, Oakland Museum of Art \, the de Young Museum\, San José Mu
 seum of Art\, Monterey Museum of Art\, Missoula Museum of Art\, National M
 useum of American Jewish History\, and the National Museum of Women in the
  Arts\, Washington\, DC. At the same time\, our friends at IceHouse Galler
 y will hold a companion exhibition of Storer’s Works on Paper. Exhibitio
 n dates are March 7 - March 28. Sunday\, April 12\, 4-5 PM Related Event: 
 In Conversation With Inez Storer Moderated by Donna Seager More Info .fe-b
 lock-fbd645bc26b960157ff2 {mix-blend-mode: \; }
LOCATION:230 Lakeville Street\, Petaluma\, CA  94952
URL:https://petalumaartscenter.org/events-exhibitions/inez-storer
X-SOURCE:Petaluma Arts Center
END:VEVENT
