 : "square" } ] In the Mirror: The Origin Stories Project with Gen Z Editio
 n Exhibition Dates: May 7 - June 6\, 2026 Opening Reception: Thursday\, Ma
 y 7\, 5:30-7:30pm Through fifty Stories + Art Boxes\, artists reflect narr
 atives of heritage\, arrival\, adversity\, resilience\, and belonging—in
 viting viewers to examine how identity is shaped by lived experience. .fe-
 block-635d83d9438605f6fa53 {mix-blend-mode: \; } [ { "type": "highlight"\,
  "id": "b4413bba-8068-4825-bc86-e6a2c46bbe60"\, "shape": "underline"\, "is
 Front": false\, "isAnimationEnabled": false\, "animation": "draw"\, "durat
 ion": 0.5\, "direction": "right"\, "color": { "type": "THEME_COLOR" }\, "t
 hickness": { "unit": "em"\, "value": 0.1 }\, "linecap": "square" } ] The O
 rigin Stories Project weaves together storytelling and visual art to explo
 re identity\, connection\, and the shared human experience. Each work begi
 ns with a personal story\, an identity-shaping moment of legacy\, arrival\
 , adversity\, or revelation.&nbsp\; It is then transformed into a Stories 
 + Art Box\, where voice and visual expression are experienced together. At
  its core\, the project is grounded in a simple belief: when people share 
 their stories and truly listen to one another\, connection grows. This exh
 ibition brings together works from the permanent collection alongside a Ge
 n Z showcase of Northern California students in the North Gallery behind y
 ou.&nbsp\; It offers an intergenerational perspective on resilience\, self
 -discovery\, and belonging. For many of these young artists\, this is the 
 first time their voices are presented in a public\, museum-quality setting
 . In a time marked by rapid change and growing disconnection\, this work c
 reates space to pause\, reflect\, and express\, building confidence and a 
 deeper sense of self. Elaine Tajima Johnston\, Curator\, Saffron Arts &amp
 \; Culture .fe-block-fe127d8f7d32c350758f {mix-blend-mode: \; } RECEPTION 
 RSVP #block-yui_3_17_2_1_1776037261529_3293 {--sqs-block-content-flex: 0\;
  } #block-yui_3_17_2_1_1776037261529_3293 { --opacity: 100%\; --translate-
