UID:a57cfef4459ed325d7c9e696db4e38f1@petalumaartscenter.org
DESCRIPTION:In dialogue with our upcoming Origin Stories exhibition\, this
  workshop uses found imagery\, vintage ephemera\, and contemporary materia
 ls to reflect on memory\, place\, and the textures of everyday life. Parti
 cipants will create layered works that balance personal narrative with bro
 ader cultural reference. Emphasis will be placed on editing\, composition\
 , and allowing materials to suggest meaning rather than working toward a f
 ixed outcome. All experience levels are welcome. Instructors : Robin Borel
 li\, Laura Engdahl\, and Jen Siddens May 16\, 2026 12:00pm – 4:00pm $150
  Members\, $170 Non-Members Materials Included Materials : Included in the
  ticket price. Participants are also encouraged to bring copies of persona
 l photographs\, letters\, maps\, or printed matter that feel connected to 
 their own sense of personal history. Buy Tickets #block-yui_3_17_2_1_17760
